Package: ggchunk
Type: Package
Title: Fold Long or High ggplot2 Graphics into One Figure
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Nuan", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "yinlin2824@gmail.com")
Author: Nuan [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Nuan <yinlin2824@gmail.com>
Description: Adds a '+ ggchunk()' verb to ggplot2 pipelines that automatically
    folds overly long or high graphics into one multi-segment figure.
    Wide x axes are drawn as consecutive rows and high y axes as consecutive
    columns. The number of segments can be set explicitly or chosen
    automatically from the plot's mappings and data. Existing facets, themes,
    scales and layers are preserved; the result is a regular ggplot or a
    patchwork composition when the package is available.
